<title>SINGAPORE: Clipsal 1996 net profit up 14.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Clipsal 1996 net profit up 14.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  23.24    vs	20.25</p>
<p>    Final divident (cents)	   5.88    vs	 5.63</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		 25.50    vs	22.40</p>
<p>    Group shr (fully diluted)     22.70    vs	19.80</p>
<p>    Turnover			   178.93    vs     151.47</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest    1.43    vs	 1.69</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		 3.83    vs	 3.56</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	   6.58    vs	 5.19</p>
<p>    Income from associates	   8.81    vs	 9.20</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    22.15    vs	17.77</p>
<p>    Tax				    6.99    vs	 5.76</p>
<p>    Minorities (loss)		  0.73    vs	 0.96</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		   11.14    vs	 1.65</p>
<p>Note - Clipsal Industries (Holdings) Ltd is an electrical fittings firm.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
